-- title:
--   Descent of an integral q-expansion to a subfield K
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$, a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, an integer $N\ge 1$, a field $k$ of characteristic $q$ and a ring homomorphism $\mathrm{red}\colon A\to k$, together with an intermediate field $K$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$. Write $A_K$ for `NodeLocalized.coeffSubring A K`, the subring $A\cap K$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, and $\overline{\mathrm{red}}$ for `NodeLocalized.redRestrict red K`, the composite of the inclusion $A_K\subseteq A$ with $\mathrm{red}$; `coeffMap` denotes coefficientwise application of a ring homomorphism to formal Laurent series (Hahn series over $\mathbb Z$). Let $h_0$ be a Laurent series over $A_K$ and $y_1$ a Laurent series over $A$ such that the image of $y_1$ in $\overline{\mathbb Q}((\mathfrak q))$ lies in `modularFunctionFieldBar N`, the intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb Q}((\mathfrak q))/\overline{\mathbb Q}$ generated by the coefficientwise images of `modularFunctionFieldFull N` $=\mathbb Q(\text{divisorExpansions } N)$, and such that the coefficientwise reduction of $h_0$ along $\overline{\mathrm{red}}$ equals that of $y_1$ along $\mathrm{red}$. Assume moreover that this image of $y_1$ is integral over the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-subalgebra of `modularFunctionFieldBar N` generated by the two elements `coeffEmb` $(\mathrm{jq})$ and `coeffEmb` $(\mathrm{qExpand}\ \mathbb Q\ N\ \mathrm{jq})$, where $\mathrm{jq}=X^{-1}\cdot\mathrm{jNumQ}$ and `qExpand` is the substitution $X\mapsto X^{N}$ on exponents. Then there exist a Laurent series $y$ over $A_K$ and an element $g$ of `modularFunctionFieldBar N` such that: $g$, viewed in $\overline{\mathbb Q}((\mathfrak q))$, lies in `NodeLocalized.fieldOver N K`, the subfield generated by the constant series attached to elements of $K$ together with `jqModC` $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ and `jqNModC` $\overline{\mathbb Q}\ N$; the coefficientwise image of $y$ in $\overline{\mathbb Q}((\mathfrak q))$ equals $g$; the reductions of $h_0$ and of $y$ along $\overline{\mathrm{red}}$ agree; and $g$ is again integral over that same $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-subalgebra generated by `coeffEmb` $(\mathrm{jq})$ and `coeffEmb` $(\mathrm{qExpand}\ \mathbb Q\ N\ \mathrm{jq})$.
--
--   This is the descent step for $\mathfrak q$-expansions in the analysis of modular curves at a node: an $A$-integral expansion of a modular function of level $N$ whose reduction already comes from $A\cap K$ is replaced, without changing the reduction or the integrality over $\overline{\mathbb Q}[j,j_N]$, by one whose constants lie in $K$. It is used by [`ModularCurve.exists_fieldOver_lift_isIntegral_of_isIntegral`](thm.html#ModularCurve.exists_fieldOver_lift_isIntegral_of_isIntegral).
